⭐ AWS LB and S






>> Load Balancing kaise kaam karta hai?
Load Balancer users ki requests ko alag-alag servers par bhejta hai, taaki ek server par zyada load na aaye.
🔥 Simple Flow
Users 👨‍💻👩‍💻 → Load Balancer 🚦 → EC2 Servers 🖥️🖥️🖥️

- User website par request bhejta hai.
- Request Load Balancer ke paas aati hai.
- Load Balancer servers ka health check karta hai.
- Load Balancer request ko healthy EC2 instance par bhejta hai.
- Server request process karke user ko response deta hai.

Example: Maan lo 1000 users website use kar rahe hain aur hamare paas 3 EC2 instances hain.
Load Balancer: 1000 Users → EC2-1 + EC2-2 + EC2-3

Agar EC2-1 down ❌ ho jaye, Load Balancer traffic ko EC2-2 aur EC2-3 par send karega ✅.

>> AWS LB type
Image me AWS Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) ke 3 types dikhaye gaye hain.
⭐ ALB — Application Load Balancer
HTTP aur HTTPS traffic ko distribute karta hai.
👉 Websites aur web applications ke liye.
Example: User → ALB → Web Servers
Works on: Layer 7 — Application Layer
Protocols: HTTP, HTTPS

⭐ NLB — Network Load Balancer
Bahut fast aur heavy network traffic handle karta hai.
👉 High performance applications ke liye.
Example: Millions of Requests → NLB → Servers

⭐ GWLB — Gateway Load Balancer
Network security ke liye use hota hai.
👉 Firewall aur security appliances ke saath.
Example: Traffic → GWLB → Firewall → Application





⭐ AWS ELB 




>> creating ELB
1. Create EC2 Instances — 2 ya usse zyada EC2 instances banao aur web server install karo.
2. Configure Security Group — HTTP aur SSH traffic allow karo.
3. Create Load Balancer — Application Load Balancer (ALB) create karo.
4. Register Targets — EC2 instances ko Target Group me add karo aur health check set karo.
5. Test Load Balancer — ALB ka DNS name browser me open karke check karo.
6. Result — Load Balancer traffic ko multiple EC2 instances me distribute karega.


⭐ ASG 
AWS ASG (Auto Scaling Group) is a service that automatically adds or removes EC2 instances based on demand to keep your application always available.

It scales up when traffic is high and scales down when traffic is low, helping to save costs and maintain the right number of servers.

